    "description": "Introduced, cool-season, perennial herb with stem reduced, appearing absent. Rhizomes are to 10 cm long, with rounded segments, woody and covered with the old leaf bases; bulbs and bulbils absent. Leaves are crowded at the apex of the rhizome and 3-foliolate; leaflets are obcordate, bilobed, 9–15 mm long and petiolate. Flowerheads are 3-30+-flowered. Petals are 10–15 mm long and pink or purple. Fruit are not known in Australia. A native of South America, it is a naturalised garden escape found on roadsides."
